  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combating Social Exclusion and Climate Change Impact on Dalit and Minority Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#xa0;&#x201c;Combating Social Exclusion and Climate Change Impact on Dalit and Minority Communities&#x201d;&#xa0;aims to promote the rights and inclusion of coastal minority communities by strengthening their capacity to assert rights, building resilience against climate change impacts, and ensuring improved access to essential services. The duration of the project is December 2024- November 2025. &#xa0;Through targeted interventions, the project will empower Dalit and minority communities in coastal areas to better understand and claim their human and legal rights, enhance resilience against climate-related challenges, and improve their access to services that enhance quality of life. The capacity of local CSOs, volunteers, and Minority Rights Promoters (MRPs) will be developed to address issues such as human rights, legal advocacy, climate resilience, Sexual and Reproductive Health Rights (SRHR), and access to services.</narrative>
  </description>
